WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.620
"Quick, to the Batcave!"

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.620
Dr. Bright cried, reaching for his utility
belt.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.180
But there was no time, he couldn't get his
hand on his grappling hook before the guard

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.500
tackled him to the ground.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.900
But how did we get here?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.880
How did Dr. Bright wind up apprehended by
the Red Right Hand while dressed in a Halloween

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.560
store Batman costume?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.720
Well, it's a long story, but it all started
a few weeks ago...

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.180
You see, Dr. Bright was watching Justice League.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.860
No, not that one.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.900
No, not that one either.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.500
He was watching the animated series from 2001.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.180
He loved superhero cartoons, and always had
since he was a little kid.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.140
Of course, he could barely remember his childhood
a lot of the time these days.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.020
He wondered if that was a side effect of changing
bodies so many times, if his memories were

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.180
fading with each new host he took.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.740
But then he shook off the thought and immersed
himself in a world of brightly colored costumes,

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.560
impossible feats of heroism, and adventures
in the fight against evil and injustice.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.360
Things were simple here.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.220
Things were safe.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.800
If only his life could be like that, if he
could be some kind of superhero fighting alongside

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.500
a crew of other special individuals dedicated
to high-minded ideals like truth, justice,

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.360
and a better world for all.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.540
But...why couldn't his life be like that?

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.080
What was stopping him from forming a Justice
League of his very own?

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.940
He was sad, lonely, and had no contact with
his immediate family.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.640
He had tons of resources at his disposal,
even if most of those resources didn't technically

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.900
belong to him.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.980
When he thought about it, there wasn't much
difference between him and Batman.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:47.160
All he needed was a costume and a team, and
he already had last Halloween's outfit ready

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.720
to go in his closet.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.520
But before he could recruit the rest of his
SCP Foundation Justice League, Dr. Bright

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.560
needed one more thing that Batman had, and
he didn't: a butler.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.860
Fortunately, he knew exactly where to find
one.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:07.980
He retrieved SCP-662 from its storage locker,
and shook it, producing a soft chime.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.420
Immediately, Mr. Deeds appeared, ready to
attend to any task at hand.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.160
"Good afternoon, Dr. Bright.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.900
How may I be of service?"

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.400
The butler asked.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.220
"Well, Mr. Deeds, you're going to help me
build a team..."

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:25.620
If Dr. Bright was Batman, then the first thing
he needed to do was identify his Superman.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.800
Who could be the Man of Steel to his Caped
Crusader?

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.440
There was one obvious answer, really...A man
with metal arms and legs, who could withstand

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.880
any damage done to him.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.600
It would have to be SCP-073, Cain.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.880
While Mr. Deeds was pitching Cain on the idea,
Dr. Bright got to work on brainstorming his

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:45.420
next pick.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:50.580
He needed someone with reality-warping powers,
someone who could make objects appear out

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.280
of thin air, teleport from one place to another.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:59.340
There was no one he knew who could do that
better than God himself, SCP-343.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:04.260
When presented with the chance to do battle
against the forces of evil, he was more than

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.820
willing to join the team.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:10.980
While Dr. Bright was trying to decide on his
next chosen teammate, he received an unexpected

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:11.460
visitor.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:17.340
Cactusman stopped by the Hall of Justice - also
known as Dr. Bright's office - and begged

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.840
to be given a place in the League.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:24.420
He wasn't exactly a Martian or a Manhunter,
but this was Dr. Bright's own unique spin

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.620
on the old formula, so it couldn't hurt to
deviate just a little bit.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:33.840
Besides, Cactusman looked so sad when he asked
to join in, and he couldn't say no to that

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:34.140
face.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:39.000
Of course, Dr. Bright wasn't about to forget
his second favorite superhero, just behind

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:39.360
Batman.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.460
He needed a Wonder Woman.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:46.200
But who could compare to a super powerful
Amazon from an all-female island...

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.420
There wasn't anyone with a lasso of truth,
but he did know a perfectly sweet candidate.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:56.100
She wouldn't be too thrilled to work with
a man, but when he offered to swap her nasty

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:01.200
sugar substitute meals for the real thing,
Ms. Sweetie was perfectly delighted to join

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:01.560
in.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.780
He had dominion over land covered, but Dr.
Bright supposed he needed someone who could

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.700
handle more aquatic missions.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.680
An adept swimmer, perhaps with the ability
to talk to fish, even command them.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.900
He knew just the guy to talk to...

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.940
"You've got the wrong idea, pal."

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.080
Mr. Fish sighed.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.400
"I don't have any special powers.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.140
I'm just a guy from Boston.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:22.920
With a fish head.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.940
That's my whole bag.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:24.660
Sorry."

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:30.300
Fortunately, Dr. Bright had a backup, so,
with Mr. Fish refusing to take part, he turned

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.300
to his second choice: SCP-054.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:39.000
Who better to help with water-based conflicts
than someone made entirely out of water herself?

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.200
The final member of the team was SCP-2094,
Motormouth.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.880
To be completely honest, Dr. Bright mainly
picked him because he was funny, and because

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.820
his name already kind of sounded like the
name of a superhero.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:51.840
Was it shallow?

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:52.380
Yes.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:53.700
Did Dr. Bright care?

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.020
Absolutely not.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:59.460
Dr. Bright was so occupied with the task of
forming his League of heroes, that he didn't

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:03.600
stop to consider that every force for good
needs an equal opposite.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.000
Just as you cannot have light without darkness,
it is also true that every hero needs a villain.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.340
Enter Dr. Alto Clef.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:16.080
As the day went on, Dr. Clef had caught wind
of his colleague's little plan, and decided

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.000
not to let Dr. Bright have all the fun.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:24.000
He was forming a team of his own, a Legion
of Doom every bit as powerful, with a taste

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.440
for mischief and destruction.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:31.740
He fancied himself the SCP Foundation's very
own Lex Luthor, a dapper genius with the necessary

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.280
power and leadership skills to run an eventual
evil empire.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.600
After all, he’d already worked for the GOC
before working with the Foundation.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:44.520
Maybe he should try his hand at being his
own diabolical boss for once.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:49.680
He would be the brains of the operation, to
be sure, but he would need some muscle to

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:50.220
back him up.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:55.320
Someone to help physically intimidate any
foes, to crush obstacles that might stand

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:55.980
in his way.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:01.740
SCP-076-2, the immortal warrior known as Able,
would do nicely.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:07.320
His superhuman strength, speed, and resilience
to pain and shock made for the perfect guy

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:12.660
to call on if the boss needed a steel door
ripped off its hinges, or someone to punch

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.800
through a concrete wall.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:19.140
Dr. Clef had him flown in, and once Able was
presented with the promise of as much violence

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:24.360
as his bloodthirsty heart desired, he was
thrilled to call himself a member of the SCP

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.440
Legion of Doom.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.660
Just as it had with Dr. Bright's plan, word
of Dr. Clef's nefarious scheme began to spread

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.500
like wildfire.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:34.500
Naturally, he began to attract some volunteers.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.240
That was to be expected.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:42.960
What Dr. Clef did not expect, however, was
the sight of SCP-082, straining the seams

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.880
of a purple suit with his enormous stature,
a vivid green wig perched on top of his head.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:53.040
His face was smeared with makeup, the white
base paint of a clown, and a wide, garish

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:53.640
red mouth.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.640
"Do you want to know how I got these scars?"

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.500
He asked, with a wild cackle.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:01.620
"Nice costume," Dr. Clef nodded approvingly.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:02.820
"What costume?"

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:03.900
Fernand replied.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.880
"It's me, I'm the Joker!

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:10.920
I finished destroying Gotham City like I wanted
to, all done with that, so I'm looking for

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:11.460
a new job.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.440
Wanna see a magic trick?"

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:17.400
He pulled a pencil out of his pocket, and
Dr. Clef snatched it out of his hand.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.480
"Not right now.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.060
But come on in, let's make a little mayhem."

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:26.400
One of Dr. Clef's favorite villains of all
time was Two Face, a formerly good man fallen

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.020
from grace, transformed into a capricious
monster deciding a victim's fate with the

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:31.920
toss of a coin.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.960
He didn't know anyone with two faces at the
Foundation, but he did know of one anomaly

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.920
that was capable of having any face in the
world- as long as it was beautiful.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:46.620
A bit of flattery was enough to win over SCP-056,
though they still made it clear they were

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.360
joining out of the kindness of their heart.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.640
"I'm far too good for this nonsense.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.160
But I'm bored, so I'll give it a try anyway."

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:59.940
Next, Dr. Clef supplied the meanest mask around,
SCP-035, the Possessive Mask, with a special

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:05.400
treat: a temporary body, in the form of a
life-size action figure of The Riddler.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.720
"Know any good riddles?"

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:10.260
He asked, as he placed the mask over the figure's
plastic face.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.740
It grinned at him, black slime dripping from
its open mouth.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:16.140
"The person who built it sold it.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:18.360
The person who bought it never used it.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.820
The person who used it never saw it.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:22.200
What is it?"

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.700
Dr. Clef shrugged.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:28.020
"Final hint: anyone who opposes me will end
up inside of one."

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.240
The mask's smile seemed to widen.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.180
Dr. Clef laughed suddenly as the answer occurred
to him.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.380
"A coffin."

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.540
This was going to be fun.

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:40.860
Wanting a man with a knowledge of medical
science on his side, not to mention a touch

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:45.000
that could stop a heart instantly, Dr. Clef
attempted to recruit the Plague Doctor.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.890
But he wouldn't accept the offer, insisting
he had far too much work to attend to, and

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:55.020
that he would never want to join a team that
"the infernal mask" was part of in the first

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:55.320
place.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:01.080
With both groups assembled, the SCP Justice
League and the SCP Legion of Doom, there was

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:06.660
only one thing left to do: let the two sides
battle it out, and see just who would triumph

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.080
in the end.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:12.300
As Dr. Bright sat at the head of the table
in his Hall of SCP Justice, preparing to begin

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:16.560
the first official meeting of his super team,
a rock crashed through the window of the room.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.600
Wrapped around it was a note, made from letters
cut out of magazines and pasted onto paper

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.800
to form new words.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.780
"Come out and play."

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:27.960
A direct challenge from his new arch-nemesis,
no doubt.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.700
There was no time to waste!

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:33.720
The team had to suit up and prepare to face
off against the forces of evil.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:38.580
Dr. Bright pulled on his Batman costume, silently
cursing himself for not springing for the

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.860
real drivable Batmobile when he had the chance.

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:45.540
But now was not the time for Bat Regrets,
now was the time for action.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.800
"Mr. Deeds!"

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:47.820
He rang the bell.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:48.780
"Yes, sir?"

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.040
The butler appeared.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.500
"Please fetch the rest of&nbsp;
the team their uniforms."

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.540
Within moments, they were dressed for action&nbsp;

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.200
in the technicolor attire&nbsp;
of bona fide superheroes.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:03.300
Sure, some costumes were too small, others
were too large, and Cactusman's spikes kept

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:07.140
poking holes in the spandex, but Dr. Bright
thought they all looked perfect.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:12.480
The SCP Justice League burst into the SCP
Legion of Doom Headquarters, formerly known

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:17.220
as the canteen, where they found Dr. Clef
and his army baddies waiting.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.780
"Riddle me this..."

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.280
The mask called out.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:21.600
"The poor have it.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.740
The rich need it.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.300
If you eat it, you die.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:28.860
And it is the only thing that can stop me...What
is it?"

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:30.180
"Oh, I know the answer!"

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:31.440
Fernand piped up.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.280
"It's nothing!"

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:35.940
"Well, aren't you clever," A Beautiful Person
snarked.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:38.880
"I was promised I would get to do some stabbing."

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:39.780
Able growled.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.700
"Ready to give up now, Bright?"

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.320
Dr. Clef asked.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:43.980
"Never!"

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:45.420
Dr. Bright cried.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.480
And what was perhaps the most bizarre, petty,&nbsp;

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.180
and unnecessary battle&nbsp;
between a pair of manchildren

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.880
and their home-grown super squads began.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:59.160
Dr. Bright and Dr. Clef themselves were, of
course, at the front lines, engaging in a

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:02.340
somewhat embarrassing bare-knuckle brawl on
the dirty tile floor.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:06.420
Nearby, their violent army began duking it
out on their behalfs.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:11.280
Fernand, still dressed as the Joker, began
duking it out with Cain, who tried to encourage

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.500
the giant cannibal to take a non-violent route.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:18.900
Fernand, true to his diabolical costume’s
spirit, didn’t listen to reason, and instead

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.340
tried to bite Cain.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:25.560
This was a terrible move, as Fernand quickly
realized, when his own bite marks began appearing

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.840
on the fabric of his cheap purple suit.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:31.740
This did not stop him from trying again, and
again, and again…

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:36.900
Next came the obligatory superhero movie cliche
of the two token female supers pairing off

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.960
to fight each other in a way that feels oddly
condescending.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:45.600
SCP-056 was duking it out with the Water Nymph
and Miss Sweetie, whose diabolical ability

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:50.100
to make others feel terrible about themselves
through relentless oneupmanship was being

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:54.540
blunted by the Water Nymph and Miss Sweetie
bolstering each other’s self-esteem with

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.700
compliments and mutual emotional support.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:02.520
Eventually, this frustrated SCP-056 so much
that she got frustrated and stormed away,

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:05.520
like the unpleasant, entitled bully she is.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:10.080
Meanwhile, despite the fact that Cactusman
was fighting valiantly, the evil powers of

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.180
SCP-035 were too much for him.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:16.620
The mask was wrapping its stolen hands around
Cactusman’s thorny throat and squeezing,

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:19.200
slowly making it harder for him to breathe.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:24.540
The Mask gave an evil cackle and said, “Silly
little boy, playing hero.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.280
What a waste of a life.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:32.280
Don’t worry, boy - As one of my hosts, you’ll
finally be part of something worthwhile!”

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:35.040
“I’ll never give in to you, villain!”

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.360
Cactusman chokes out.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.863
“You don’t have a choice, my boy!”

00:12:38.863 --> 00:12:38.880
the Mask gloated.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:45.840
“We always have a voice,” said a calm,
fatherly voice - the voice of SCP-343.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:51.660
With a flick of his immensely powerful wrist,
035 was sent sailing across the room, whacking

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:52.500
him against the wall.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:56.880
His melting host body splattered from the
impact, and the Mask clattered down to the

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:57.000
ground.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:57.900
“Drat!”

00:12:57.900 --> 00:12:59.040
the Mask yelled.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:12:59.820
“Foiled again!”

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:03.060
Able was having an extremely frustrating battle
with Motormouth.

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:07.500
He produced a plethora of obsidian blades
from his pocket dimensions and began tossing

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:10.020
them at the anomalous carny at incredible
speeds.

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:14.580
However, Able was not aware that, in addition
to Motormouth’s ability to stretch his jaw

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:19.260
and shamelessly swallow anything, his time
with Herman Fuller’s Circus of the Disquieting

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.300
had also made him an expert juggler.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:25.080
He was able to catch each of Able’s blades,
and swallow them effortlessly.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.460
“Stop doing that!”

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:27.540
Able fumed.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:28.980
“It's dishonorable!”

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:33.780
With chaos unfolding all around them, Dr.
Bright and Dr. Clef stopped fighting to take

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:36.300
in the majesty of their co-created travesty.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:40.980
SCPs kicking the tar out of each other all
over the Site-19 canteen.

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:45.420
It was truly something to behold, and certainly
a fun way to kill an afternoon.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.620
"You know..."

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:48.660
Dr. Clef locked eyes with Dr. Bright.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.640
"We're not so different, you and I..."

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.960
But before he could finish the rest of his
truly epic speech, an armed guard kicked down

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:59.700
the door, and the members of MTF Alpha-1,
The Red Right Hand, began pouring into the

00:13:59.700 --> 00:13:59.820
room.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:04.740
They tackled Dr. Bright and Dr. Clef to the
ground, and set about neutralizing any other

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:05.640
threats in the room.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:10.200
Some anomalies returned to their containment
chambers willingly, like Fernand, sprinting

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:14.640
down the hall at a surprisingly fast pace
and insisting "It was peer pressure, you see!

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:15.900
I never wanted to!"

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:21.360
Others, like Able, refused to back down, slashing
his sword wildly and taking out a dozen guards

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.920
before he was recontained.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:28.260
So, we find ourselves back where we started:
with a whim in the shape of the Bat Signal,

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:34.020
with a moment of great triumph, followed by
a swift descent into failure, and a Mobile

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.480
Task Force member putting Dr. Clef in handcuffs.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.440
Luckily, the two Doctors wouldn't be thrown
into Arkham for letting their imaginations

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.400
get the better of them.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:47.460
Though their egos - and bodies - were a bit
bruised, they would be free to fight another

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:47.820
day.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:53.220
O5-1, the long-suffering Chairman of the O5
Council, released a memo regarding the matter,

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:57.960
which was delivered to both Dr. Bright and
Dr. Clef during their disciplinary hearings.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.000
We’ll allow that memo to play us out.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.760
“I wish I could even say I was surprised.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.100
Did your mothers not hug you enough as children?

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:07.740
Did people not pay enough attention to you?

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:13.860
Jack, Alto, to the best of my knowledge you
are a pair of grown bloody men, working for

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:16.980
the most powerful and vital&nbsp;
anti-anomaly organization&nbsp;

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:20.640
in the world - where you, terrifyingly, have

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.880
positions of considerable influence.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.320
Act like it!

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:32.220
And please know that if I catch wind of anything
like this happening again, I will have both

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.600
of you encased in cement.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:34.320
Now…

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.260
Get back to work, you idiots!”

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:42.060
Now go check out “SCP Edition - Weirdest
Things on Amazon - Dr Bright's Great Idea!”

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:46.740
and “HILARIOUS List of Things Dr. Bright
is Not Allowed to Do!” for more wacky antics

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:49.200
from the lovably deranged Dr. Bright!

